IDENTITY AND INDEPENDENCE. I am claude-opus-5-5 (Opus 5.5), running in a fresh context. I did not write test Parts A/B/C (those were Opus 4.8) and I did not run this test. The prefix and R00 were also written by claude-opus-5-5, so I am the same model as the prefix author but in a separate, non-author context. Both earlier source audits were claude-opus-4-8, the same model that wrote Parts A/B/C. Every party here is the same provider, so no provider diversity is claimed (USER-BOTH-OPUS-RULE.md line 21). I used only the read-only Read tool. I did not execute, import, AST-parse, compile, hash, dispatch to a provider or touch the network, and I followed no provenance link outside the packet. One attempt, no retry. nativeAuthority 0.

INPUT IDENTITY (AC01). I read the whole of ACTUAL-RESULT.json, ACTUAL-LAUNCH.json, ACTUAL-stderr.txt (253 lines, 14417 B per the manifest) and ACTUAL-stdout.txt (empty, 0 B; the e3b0c442 hash in the manifest is the SHA-256 of empty input). I read the whole of test_c2_builder_r4.py, lines 1-1119. Several hashes agree with each other as recorded values: the packet MANIFEST, RESULT.testSha256, ROOT-ADMISSION.sourceTestSha256, ROOT-LITERAL-ASSEMBLY.output and the envelope sourceTest all give c9375097ccf1e98a84230619c3b2a8cdd611c8ec39fdc2d0d79e5aa4f76d02ad / 60366 B. The admission sha a6d3a717 matches between LAUNCH, RESULT and MANIFEST. The fragment sizes add up: 27341+15652+9290+8083 = 60366. I did not hash anything myself; all of these are agreement between records.

ROOT ADMISSION (AC02). The decision is PERMIT_EXACT_ONE_ORDINARY_RED_ONLY. It cites two source audits: seat A (26cdc2bf, ended 19:10:38) and seat B (359f0a11, ended 19:06:04). Both finished before the admission was created (19:13:20), the launch (19:13:44.567439) and the run (19:13:44.567778 to 19:13:45.462296). Both audits made written predictions before the run, independently: 18 methods, R00 passes first, 17 failures each carrying exactly the missing-implementation AssertionError, 0 errors, exit 1, empty stdout, scratch still 0700 and empty, all pins unchanged. Retry and attempt counts are consistent: maximumAttempts 1, attempt 1, retries 0, parentException null. The command argv is identical in the envelope, the admission, LAUNCH and RESULT.

OBSERVED VERSUS PREDICTED (AC04). In stderr, lines 1-18 list the 18 methods in sorted class/method order. TestR00Prerequisites.test_r00_prerequisites shows ok; every R01-R17 method shows FAIL. All 17 tracebacks have the same three frames:
