The summary reads 18 tests in 0.149s, FAILED (failures=17), with no errors= count. Nothing else appears: no warnings, no ResourceWarning, no extra exception, no STOP RuntimeError. The tracebacks run inside the /case/isolated mount, which confirms the bwrap layout was used. The RESULT fields agree: methods 18, passes 1, failures 17, errors 0, missingAssertionLines 17, exit 1.

R00 FACTS, MEASURED VERSUS UNPROVED (AC03). Because R00 reported ok in this run, the following are measured facts on the pinned bytes under this python3.14 sandbox:
- all 7 PINS sizes and SHA-256 values match, including B9 at 308672/10baa179 (B9 was read by the test, not by me);
- r2, host_codec and legacy loaded from exactly the pinned paths;
- v1 is absent, not in sys.modules, and find_spec returns None;
- scratch was an empty 0700 directory when R00 ran;
- all five O_ flags and the six dir_fd functions are supported;
- legacy PIN_B9_APPLIED, FAMILY_V2 and AUDIT_SOURCE_PINS equal the prefix literals;
- the K6 setupRecordSha256 equals the K2 pin;
- legacy frozen_positive_cbor equals the independent env_cbor;
- BLAKE2b-256 of that CBOR equals K6_TOKEN, and SHA-256 of the proof equals K6_PROOF_SHA;
- the VK is 488 bytes and the proof 192 bytes;
- the HIST-09 bytes equal both the independent formatter and the legacy render;
