These are byte, CBOR and hash consistency facts only. They do not prove:
- Groth16 validity, curve validity or VK profile;
- circuit/VK correspondence;
- Rust acceptance;
- that the hash recipe matches what a real Cardano node computes (only internal Python BLAKE2b equality is shown);
- that the UPLC VM accepts the contexts;
- anything about the ledger, fees or ExUnits, or Preview/Preprod;
- anything beyond the single-party, TEST ONLY, forgeable setup.

The six GOVERNANCE_PINS (test lines 49-56) are root-delegated, not test-checked. RESULT records them before and after, unchanged, at the same bytes and hashes as the admission and the MANIFEST. Both audits recorded this delegation openly (Source A F04, Source B F2); it is not a silent waiver.

EFFECTS AND COMMAND (AC05). The run is ordinary only:
- timeout 20s with TERM and a 2s kill-after;
- prlimit cpu 10:10, as 536870912, fsize 2097152, core 0;
- bwrap --unshare-all --die-with-parent --new-session, with /usr read-only, isolated read-only, scratch as the only writable bind, chdir to isolated, clearenv, and only PATH, LANG and PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE set;
- /usr/bin/python3 -I -B on the test file. stdin was DEVNULL (LAUNCH).

The run took about 0.9 s, and exit code 1 is unittest's own failure code, not a timeout code such as 124 or 137. The 8 runtime file pins (bytes, SHA and mode 0444) and the 6 governance pins are identical before and after. scratchEmpty is true and scratchMode 0o700. No R4 file is among the inputs, and the MISSING path fires only when the file does not exist, so 17 observations show build_k10_inputs_r4.py was absent each time. No implementation was present or executed. Two limits on what this shows:
- rlimits are not network isolation;
- the captured --unshare-all argv is a record of what was asked for, not a broader attestation of the platform's actual namespace or isolation behaviour.

Capture through regular files rather than PIPE is stated in the capturePlan and implied by the file paths, hashes and byte counts. RESULT and LAUNCH have no explicit capture-mode field, directory-mode or listing enumeration, or post-run interpreter hash, so I treat these as root records. The output was small and complete (stderr ends with the final FAILED summary), so nothing was truncated and the fsize question does not arise.

MEANINGFULNESS (AC06). The RED meets contract section 8 and API.red: R00 passes, and R01-R17 fail only with the missing-implementation text, with 0 errors. The stub check remains a source-only prediction. Both pre-run audits predicted the same thing: a stub with the CB401 imports, the seam and 7 functions that raise NotImplementedError would load, pass R00 and R01, and pass none of R02-R17, because NotImplementedError is not a ValueError and no value comes back. I re-derived this from the source and agree. No stub was made or run, and no passing prefix was rerun. The observed RED shows only that the absence wiring works. The R01-R17 test bodies have never run, so their own correctness (for example the mkfifo in R06, umask handling in R14, and 0555 permission enforcement inside the bwrap user namespace in R16) is first exercised at GREEN.

